/* Movie Night — dataset (v4). Each movie carries a 0-10 taste vector on ten axes:
   adrenaline, brainy, scary, funny, heartwarming, dark, romantic, epic, cozy, weird.
   Entries with tier "core" are hand-written. Entries with tier "catalog" were
   sourced from Wikipedia year/genre categories: director and runtime come from
   the film's infobox (runtime is null when unknown — never invented), the
   description is adapted from the film's Wikipedia lead (CC BY-SA), and the
   taste vector is an ESTIMATE derived from genre-baseline profiles.
   Genre tags in the refined taxonomy (Psychological Thriller, Rom-Com,
   Superhero, Neo-Noir, Documentary, Historical Drama, Family Drama,
   Modern Drama, Horror Thriller, Animated) come from Wikipedia category
   evidence or the derived-label rules documented in the README.
   Poster URLs come from the Wikipedia API (verified live at build time);
   an empty poster means the UI draws an elegant generated cover instead. */
